Console1 parameter maps for the JSFX ports by chmaha, from two repositories.

Source: https://github.com/chmaha/airwindows-JSFX-ports
Source: https://github.com/chmaha/DSP-Ports-JSFX

The DSP-Ports maps are the four named "... port) by chmaha": Compressor
(x42-darc), Gate (ZamGateX2), EQ (x42-fil4) and Lumina Channel Strip. Those
plugins shipped with REAPER 7.83 and were removed again in 7.84, so users now
need them from ReaPack.


NEEDS CHECKING: parameter indices of the DSP-Ports maps
-------------------------------------------------------

The four DSP-Ports maps were written by reading the slider declarations in the
JSFX sources rather than by reading parameter indices out of REAPER, on the
assumption that a JSFX slider N is parameter index N-1. The index listings in
the older maps here agree with that, but it has not been verified against a
running REAPER.

To check: open any one of the four, look at what the mapping panel reports for
a control, and compare with the index listing in the comments at the bottom of
that map's .ini. If the assumption is wrong it is wrong by a constant offset,
so all four are wrong in the same way and each is a one-line-per-entry fix.

Two judgement calls in those maps are also worth a second opinion, and both are
commented where they occur:

- EQ (x42-fil4): Eq_hp_shape and Eq_lp_shape are on the Low Shelf Enable and
  High Shelf Enable rather than on the filter resonances, because on the
  hardware those buttons switch the LF and HF bands between shelf and bell.
- Gate (ZamGateX2): Shp_sustain is on Max Gate Close, as the nearest
  continuous analogue to how far the gate closes, and Shp_hard_gate is on the
  Gate/Duck mode switch because it is a button on the hardware.


Dry/wet and bypass
------------------

Several maps here point Comp_DryWet or Comp_comp at a plugin's own mix or
bypass slider. REAPER also exposes its own per-FX wet and bypass controls,
which every FX has whether or not the plugin provides them, and which would be
the better target. They cannot be written into these files as they stand:
mapping values are parsed as plain integers, and REAPER's wet and bypass have
no fixed index — they are resolved per FX instance through
TrackFX_GetParamFromIdent with ":wet" or ":bypass". Supporting them needs that
resolution step in the loader, after which a map could say Comp_DryWet=:wet.
Until then an unparseable value reads as unmapped, so writing it now would
silently do nothing.
